setShown fires only when the manager adds or removes a building, and each fire re-renders App

Try removing 'cast-shadows': true from the sun light.

Batch setShown updates (collect adds/removes and apply once per tick) if the manager emits many at a time

setInterval(() => ('manager', managerRef.current?.stats()), 3000) uses the comma operator, so it calls stats() but never logs. You want console.log('manager', ...).

Character.tsx uses the BuildingColliderManager type but doesn’t import it. Also, the red mesh has scale={5} while the CapsuleCollider isn’t scaled, so the visual is 5x bigger than the physical body

Nothing in your code draws or moves the mesh directly. Its position changes because it is a child of the RigidBody, and @react-three/rapier copies the physics body’s transform onto the three.js object after each physics step

r3f-perf is already in your project. Its draw calls and frame counters show whether rendering is continuous.

Setting frameloop="demand" on the Canvas, if react-three-map allows it, would show whether the render loop stops when nothing changes

With state, the onClick closure would capture the manager value from when the effect ran and could go stale. With a ref, managerRef.current always gives the latest manager

